# Debounced Async API Call with Cancellation

Here's a comprehensive implementation with multiple approaches:

## Basic Implementation with AbortController

```javascript
function createDebouncedAsyncCall(asyncFn, delay = 300) {
  let timeoutId = null;
  let abortController = null;

  return async function debounced(...args) {
    // Cancel previous request
    if (abortController) {
      abortController.abort();
    }

    // Clear previous timeout
    if (timeoutId) {
      clearTimeout(timeoutId);
    }

    // Create new abort controller for this call
    abortController = new AbortController();

    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
      timeoutId = setTimeout(async () => {
        try {
          const result = await asyncFn(...args, {
            signal: abortController.signal,
          });
          resolve(result);
        } catch (error) {
          if (error.name === 'AbortError') {
            reject(new Error('Request was cancelled'));
          } else {
            reject(error);
          }
        }
      }, delay);
    });
  };
}
```

